cinity of grain boundaries in the matrix."},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","label":"text","orig":"Microstructural examinations from previous studies have shown that the favored sites for the formation of phases are grain boundaries and the reinforcement/matrix interface [27]. The phase of iron nitride formed in the XRD result (Fig. 2) is obviously due to the diffusion of iron and nitride at the grain boundary as indicated in the EDS result (Fig. 3b1). It is worthy to state that during the SPS process, non-equilibrium conditions exists in the material, which has a significant influence on diffusion and the reactions taking place during sintering. The formation of FeN0.068 phase in the studied composites is as a result of intense phenomena taking place during SPS (surface activation, diffusion, surface melting, necking between the particles of sintered powder, and plastic flow [28]). During sintering, mass transport increases and eventually results in","parent":{"$ref":"#/body"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":489.7790852070312,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":47.373999999999995,"r":286.4674567,"t":647.2650324070313},"charspan":[0,865],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/3","text":"Microstructural examinations from previous studies have shown that the favored sites for the formation of phases are grain boundaries and the reinforcement/matrix interface [27]. The phase of iron nitride formed in the XRD result (Fig. 2) is obviously due to the diffusion of iron and nitride at the grain boundary as indicated in the EDS result (Fig. 3b1). It is worthy to state that during the SPS process, non-equilibrium conditions exists in the material, which has a significant influence on diffusion and the reactions taking place during sintering. The formation of FeN0.068 phase in the studied composites is as a result of intense phenomena taking place during SPS (surface activation, diffusion, surface melting, necking between the particles of sintered powder, and plastic flow [28]). During sintering, mass transport increases and eventually results in"},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","label":"caption","orig":"Fig. 4 -Effect of sintering temperature variation on the densification and hardness of DSS 2205-5TiN.","parent":{"$ref":"#/pictures/0"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":501.1532945070312,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":304.41,"r":523.8252928999999,"t":521.1542417070311},"charspan":[0,101],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/4","text":"Fig. 4 -Effect of sintering temperature variation on the densification and hardness of DSS 2205-5TiN."},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","label":"text","orig":"99.0","parent":{"$ref":"#/pictures/0"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":719.9360122070311,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":321.939,"r":333.61500000000007,"t":725.6780122070312},"charspan":[0,4],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/5","text":"99.0"},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","label":"text","orig":"295","parent":{"$ref":"#/pictures/0"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":705.2231122070311,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":519.676,"r":529.6840000000001,"t":710.9651122070312},"charspan":[0,3],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/6","text":"295"},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","label":"text","orig":"Density","parent":{"$ref":"#/pictures/0"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":712.1028022070311,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":485.54510000000005,"r":505.54910000000007,"t":717.8448022070312},"charspan":[0,7],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/7","text":"Density"},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","label":"text","orig":"Hardness","parent":{"$ref":"#/pictures/0"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":703.6028022070311,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":485.54510000000005,"r":511.2191,"t":709.3448022070312},"charspan":[0,8],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/8","text":"Hardness"},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","label":"text","orig":"290","parent":{"$ref":"#/pictures/0"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":674.0567022070311,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":519.676,"r":529.6840000000001,"t":679.7987022070312},"charspan":[0,3],"page_no":